SN CheckLevel v1.1

Compares a user's current access level with their previous level.  If
there has been a change, it'll notify them and update its records.

Quick & Easy Installation:

 1  Place it somewhere.  (PFiles: would be good.)

 2  Insert the following line somewhere in your sys.welcome (or _End if
    you're using SN_LoginConfig v3.3+):

    {#0SN:SN_CheckLevel}

    Modify the path to suit and remember, \ = CTRL-Y and { = CTRL-Q.

 3  Log on and run the program once to build it's initial files.  It
    will report it's progress and let you know when it's done.  Once
    that's done, you're good.  You can test it by using your pull-down
    menu for the stat window (or pressing RAmiga-T, modifying your
    access level then re-running the program.  It'll let you know there
    has been a change and update it's data on you.  Change your level
    back and re-run it so it'll update it's records with your correct
    access level.  That's it!

(This sucker wasn't big enough to deserve it's own .guide, installer, icons,
help file, blah blah blah plus tax...)

